adr: 0363
file: lsp/pasls.pas
kills: command-injection
why: PathArg stops refusing a path holding chr(0), so the first foreign crossing -- PasFS.Exists -- stops the server, and the request after the bad one is never answered. The gate sends exactly that pair and requires the second to be answered.
--- old
    if p[k] = chr(0) then p := '' else k := k + 1;
--- new
    if false then p := '' else k := k + 1;
